<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Danio margaritatus (Celestial Pearl Danio))",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 13.39 µm in Danio margaritatus (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Danio margaritatus (Celestial Pearl Danio) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio margaritatus (Celestial Pearl Danio) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio margaritatus (Celestial Pearl Danio)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That adult pearl spacing equals 13.39 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the convex-hull animation is a copy of the photograph.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 0.018 m catalog length applied to the pearl-field major axis.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters that set lambda_c to 1.339e-05 m for margaritatus, stability for albolineatus, and 17.80 µm for nigrofasciatus.",
        "reported_in_source: Conway, Chen & Mayden 2008: the celestial pearl danio is a miniature Danio.",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. 2009: melanophore-xanthophore interactions have the short-range activation and long-range inhibition structure of a Turing system.",
        "reported_in_source: Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: Danio species differ in how stripes and spots are deployed.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite k_c.",
        "transfer_boundary: Predecessor and successor parameters are not fits to photographs of those species.",
        "transfer_boundary: The adult photograph samples at about 21 µm per pixel, so 13.39 µm is not a direct measurement on that image." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Danio margaritatus (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/danio_margaritatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Danio margaritatus (Celestial Pearl Danio); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system can be stable at k = 0 and unstable at a finite k_c. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: melanophore-xanthophore interactions have the short-range activation and long-range inhibition structure of a Turing system. | Quigley et al. 2004 and Patterson et al. 2014: Danio species differ in how stripes and spots are deployed. | Conway, Chen & Mayden 2008: the celestial pearl danio is a miniature Danio.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters that set lambda_c to 1.339e-05 m for margaritatus, stability for albolineatus, and 17.80 µm for nigrofasciatus. | 0.018 m catalog length applied to the pearl-field major axis.; transfer_boundary: The adult photograph samples at about 21 µm per pixel, so 13.39 µm is not a direct measurement on that image. | Predecessor and successor parameters are not fits to photographs of those species.; does_not_claim: That adult pearl spacing equals 13.39 µm. | That the convex-hull animation is a copy of the photograph.]; phenomenon_size: 20 µm (2.018e-05 m, log10=-4.695 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 20 µm to 4.5 cm): 20 µm:danio-aesculapii-bioelectric-polarity, 63 µm:danio-aesculapii-vertex-packing, 1.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength, 2.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-clock-wavefront, 4.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-morphogen-condensation, 5.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-elastic-buckling, 6.3 mm:danio-aesculapii-flux-canalization, 8.8 mm:danio-aesculapii-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms6299>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05629-z>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.11646/zootaxa.1686.1.1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01526> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://daniocell.nichd.nih.gov/>,
        <https://mapzebrain.org/>,
        <https://zebrahub.ds.czbiohub.org/>,
        <https://zfin.org/> ;
    pk:fossilLineageGroup "Danionin Pigment Evolution Series" ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-margaritatus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
